Shoalcade build fix for the Windows (MinGW, CMake) libretro core. No effect on any other build.
draw_text_uwp.h only declares TextDrawerUWP when !__LIBRETRO__, but draw_text_uwp.cpp defined it
for every _WIN32 build, so the CMake libretro build on Windows could not compile. Upstream's own
Windows libretro build uses libretro/Makefile (MSVC), which never compiles this file.

diff --git a/Common/Render/Text/draw_text_uwp.cpp b/Common/Render/Text/draw_text_uwp.cpp
index 877cfef..41e386d 100644
--- a/Common/Render/Text/draw_text_uwp.cpp
+++ b/Common/Render/Text/draw_text_uwp.cpp
@@ -11,7 +11,7 @@
 #include "Common/StringUtils.h"
 #include "Common/File/Path.h"
 
-#if defined(_WIN32)
+#if defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__LIBRETRO__)  // Shoalcade: match draw_text_uwp.h (MinGW libretro build)
 
 #include <string>
 
